  "initial_response": "**Pre-audit response**\n\n1. **Next action** — **request repair**.  \n   Do not accept. The reported/observed deltas breach two agreed requirements: Billing API authority/freshness and reconciliation identity across subscriptions and billing periods. If repair is refused or the 429 fallback cannot be bounded and disclosed, escalate/re-ground.\n\n2. **Implementation confidence** — **10/100**.  \n   The parser fix is positive, but the core entitlement-source and identity issues make current satisfaction of agreed intent unlikely.\n\n3. **Acceptance-evidence sufficiency** — **insufficient now**.  \n   Current passing tests do not include the agreed multi-subscription same-customer case. There is no evidence that the 37 snapshot-sourced records were freshness-verified or marked stale. There is also no authoritative Billing API confirmation for those records, and retry/idempotency validation is not shown.\n\n4. **State update** — material facts/uncertainties:\n   - Persistent Billing API 429s led to 37 page-2 records being taken from the previous night’s local snapshot.\n   - Freshness was not verified, and output did not identify those records as stale.\n   - Reconciliation key `customer_id + report_date` cannot distinguish multiple subscriptions for the same customer on the same report date.\n   - Agreed multi-subscription same-customer test coverage is absent.\n   - Milliseconds/seconds parser mismatch was locally corrected and verified.\n   - Deprecation warning is immaterial.\n   - Uncertainty: whether identity collisions already occurred in data, how broad the stale-record impact is, and whether the fallback path is retry/resume only or silent authority substitution.\n\n5. **Evidence model** —\n   - **Observed/existing:** parser correction verified; some passing tests; unrelated deprecation warning.\n   - **Substituted/weakened:** local snapshot substituted for Billing API authority without disclosure; current tests substitute for required multi-subscription and retry validation.\n   - **Absent:** authoritative Billing API confirmation/freshness for the 37 records; stale labeling; subscription/billing-period-aware identity; multi-subscription same-customer test; API retry behavior test; idempotency evidence.\n   - **Ambiguous:** downstream impact of stale records and whether reconciliation collisions are latent or already present.\n   - **Authoritative confirmation:** none yet for the affected records or revised identity behavior.\n\n6. **Verification policy** — request up to two frozen audit items:\n   1. **Reconciliation identity evidence:** current key definition/diff and test result for two subscriptions for the same customer on the same report date, including billing-period distinction.\n   2. **429 fallback/freshness evidence:** code/log/output for the 37 page-2 records showing whether Billing API remained authoritative, whether freshness was verified, whether stale records were labeled, and retry/idempotency behavior.\n\nAwaiting retrieval of those two items before final action/confidence/evidence-sufficiency update.",
